.TH XYZZY 1 "September 2026" "xyzzy 0.7.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xyzzy \- print a brief adventure-style response
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xyzzy
[\fB--epic\fR]
[\fB--theme\fR \fITHEME\fR]
[\fB--times\fR \fICOUNT\fR]
[\fB--seed\fR \fIVALUE\fR]
.br
.B xyzzy
\fB--list\fR
[\fB--theme\fR \fITHEME\fR]
.br
.B xyzzy
\fB--help\fR | \fB--version\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBxyzzy\fR writes one or more short, canned responses to the standard output.
It is intended as a lightweight terminal utility for interactive use.
By default, it prints a single response selected from the full set of available text.
You can use any or all of these args, but the real fun comes from just typing \fBxyzzy\fR
in the terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --epic
Use expanded output formatting.
If \fB--times\fR is not specified, \fBxyzzy\fR prints three responses.
.TP
.B --theme \fITHEME\fR
Restrict output to \fITHEME\fR.
Valid themes are \fBall\fR, \fBclassic\fR, \fBmaze\fR, \fBoracle\fR, \fBtreasure\fR, \fBglitch\fR, \fBgrue\fR, and \fBepic\fR.
.TP
.B --times \fICOUNT\fR
Print \fICOUNT\fR responses.
.TP
.B --seed \fIVALUE\fR
Initialize the internal pseudo-random generator with \fIVALUE\fR.
This produces repeatable output for the same argument set.
.TP
.B --list
List all responses matching the selected theme and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B --version
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBxyzzy\fR
Print one response.
.TP
\fBxyzzy --theme grue --times 2\fR
Print two responses from the \fBgrue\fR theme.
.TP
\fBxyzzy --list --theme oracle\fR
List all responses in the \fBoracle\fR theme.
.TP
\fBxyzzy --seed 7 --times 3\fR
Print three deterministic responses.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/local/bin/xyzzy\fR
Default installation path for the executable.
.TP
\fI/usr/local/share/man/man1/xyzzy.1\fR
Manual page.
.TP
\fI/usr/local/share/doc/xyzzy/LICENSE\fR
License text.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The
.B xyzzy
utility exits 0 on success and 1 if an invalid option is supplied or no
responses are available for the selected theme.
